Bandit Level 2 - Level 3

Challenge: Read a file with spaces in its name.

Solution:

cat ./'--spaces in this filename--'

Explanation:

./ tells Linux to look for the file in the current directory.
The quotes (' ') keep the filename, including its spaces, as a single argument.
Without quotes, Linux would treat each word as a separate filename.

